WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.552
A language model

00:00:01.364 --> 00:00:02.413
just rewrote its

00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:03.085
own weights

00:00:03.606 --> 00:00:04.549
A new paper

00:00:04.361 --> 00:00:05.327
shows an open

00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:06.294
twenty-seven billion

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.308
parameter model that

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:07.863
is given its

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:08.841
weights and graded

00:00:08.653 --> 00:00:09.337
answers

00:00:09.514 --> 00:00:10.787
then diagnoses its

00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:11.636
own failures

00:00:12.166 --> 00:00:13.357
With no gradients

00:00:13.168 --> 00:00:14.182
and no training

00:00:14.371 --> 00:00:15.184
it rewrites its

00:00:14.996 --> 00:00:15.951
weights and gets

00:00:15.763 --> 00:00:16.776
six point six

00:00:16.588 --> 00:00:17.743
points more accurate

00:00:17.555 --> 00:00:18.498
on problems it

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.147
never saw

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:20.589
It can even

00:00:20.401 --> 00:00:21.533
repair a damaged

00:00:21.345 --> 00:00:22.405
copy of itself

00:00:22.217 --> 00:00:23.219
to over eighty

00:00:23.031 --> 00:00:23.844
percent of the

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.035
original accuracy

00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:26.096
and only the

00:00:25.908 --> 00:00:27.311
largest models manage

00:00:27.123 --> 00:00:27.570
it

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.124
Full story on

00:00:28.935 --> 00:00:29.831
the dashboard
